{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/docs.GrrCloneCore\/documentation\/GrrCloneCore\/MountRegistry\/loadFailure"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"loadFailure","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"? { get }","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This is not the same as an empty registry, and the difference is the whole","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"point of the type. An absent file legitimately means “nothing mounted”. An","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"unreadable one means “we do not know what we own” — and since ownership is the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only thing that authorises an unmount, treating it as “nothing” silently","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"disowns every live mount: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"owns()"},{"text":" goes false, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"shutdown()"},{"type":"text","text":" skips them, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reconcileOrphans()"},{"type":"text","text":" returns early on an empty list."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The realistic trigger is not disk damage but a schema change: add one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"non-optional field to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Entry","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and every existing record stops decoding.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/docs.GrrCloneCore\/documentation\/GrrCloneCore","doc:\/\/docs.GrrCloneCore\/documentation\/GrrCloneCore\/MountRegistry"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Set whe